OwnGit {{.Version}}
Portable archive for {{.Target}}

OwnGit keeps private Git repositories and a browser dashboard on a computer you
control. This archive is a portable build. Unpacking it does not register a
service, add anything to PATH, or write outside the directory you unpack it in.
Running it writes host-local state, described under Data below.

Requirements
  Git must be on PATH. OwnGit uses the installed Git for repository storage
  and Smart HTTP. Pull request merge requires Git 2.38 or newer, and an older
  Git refuses the merge instead of guessing.

Start
  {{.Invocation}} serve
  The first start from a terminal runs setup there. Choose English or Korean,
  then "Continue in this terminal" or "Open the web dashboard"; in the
  browser you get a short code to approve in the terminal.
  Started without a terminal, OwnGit writes an owner-readable setup file in
  the state directory, logs the file's path, and opens the file in a browser
  unless it was started with --no-open. {{.Invocation}} setup-link prints a
  new link.
  The dashboard listens on 127.0.0.1:7654 by default.

{{if .IconApp}}Menu bar icon
  OwnGit.app beside the program is the OwnGit icon in the macOS menu bar. It
  shows whether OwnGit runs, the clone address, the latest pushes and Open
  dashboard. {{.Invocation}} service install opens it in your desktop
  login, and it then opens whenever you sign in. Keep OwnGit.app next to
  {{.Binary}}, which it runs. {{.Invocation}} tray off hides it, and
  {{.Invocation}} tray on shows it again; OwnGit keeps running either way.

{{end}}Data
  Host-local state lives in the platform configuration directory under
  "owngit", or in ~/.owngit when no configuration directory is available.
  Repositories live in the storage directory chosen during setup.

Update
  {{.Invocation}} update prints the one command that replaces this program
  with the newest release. OwnGit never runs it or updates itself.

Remove
  {{.Invocation}} uninstall removes the service that "service install"
  registered, then delete this directory. Repositories and state are kept
  unless you delete them yourself.

Version
  {{.Invocation}} version

Coding tool integration
  docs/CODING_TOOLS.md  running project checks from a coding tool
  docs/CODING_TOOLS.ko.md
                        the same guide in Korean
  integrations/skills/owngit-checks/SKILL.md
                        a shared Agent Skill you can copy into a coding tool
  Installing the skill is your choice. Copy it, or run
  {{.Invocation}} skill --install DIR with the skills directory your coding
  tool scans. Nothing installs it for you otherwise.
  {{.Invocation}} is a relative invocation that works while your shell is in
  this unpacked directory. Unpacking adds nothing to PATH, so from anywhere
  else supply the actual absolute path of the {{.Binary}} file in this
  directory.

